From 7ff275fa043caead368770d4ef4b917ec58be736 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiming Pang <discrete_brain@163.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 17:56:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 32/43] smap: bulk stage-2 walk for 4K page scanning
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace per-4K-page kvm_pgtable_walk(addr, 1) calls with PMD-granularity
bulk walks that descend the upper page table levels (PGD/PUD/PMD) once
per 2MB range instead of 512 times.

Add smap_kvm_pgtable_stage2_mkold_range() in kvm_pgtable.c which walks
[addr, addr+size) via KVM_PGTABLE_WALK_LEAF | SHARED, invoking the
caller per-PTE callback for each leaf entry. The callback-based design
keeps generic PTE-level AF test/clear in kvm_pgtable.c while HVA→HPA
recording stays in accessed_bit.c.

The 4K scan loop in process_memslot_pages_4k() iterates at PMD
granularity aligned to HVA PMD boundaries via hva_to_gfn_memslot(),
ensuring each walk range falls within a single HVA PMD for correct
bloom filter keying. Non-4K (huge page) scanning continues via the
existing per-page process_memslot_pages() path unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
